     vf_ 9 -> z=u4   jac0=True disjoint-from-vm=True   Psi: identity (vf is the coord)
     vf_11 -> z=u19  jac0=True disjoint-from-vm=True   Psi: z19 := u11*u4 + u15*u6*u7 + u19
  z-coords ['u0', 'u16', 'u2', 'u17', 'u3', 'u18', 'u4', 'u19'] DISJOINT from supp(vm) & all jac-0: True

====================================================================================================
Psi (per type) = the product of unipotent shears {u_z := u_z + (vf_k - u_z)} over the LINEAR vf,
identity on the pure-monomial vf.  Block-triangular, det=1, keep-set INCLUDES supp(vm)={u1,u5,u20-images}
and every non-z coord.  Under Psi: vf_k|_{k in reg-seq} = z_j (coords); vm unchanged; jac u^kappa unchanged.
Other dominants p1: apply sigma_{p1} (loss-symmetry) to vm, kappa, the vf/z sets — r, threshold, value invariant.
